 This install applies to "Gunship" (c) 1987-1989 Microprose, 1 disk.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 18.0 to be in the path.
 It can be found in the WHDLoad package. Installation copies files from the
 original Gunship disk. Select the disk's release in the installer: PAL
 (SPS 0658), NTSC (SPS 1489), or another supported release.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem.
 For Enhanced framerate, use a 68020 or later and at least 2 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype
 "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.

 Features:
 ---------
 - Disk and password protections removed on the supported original versions.
 - Access fault fixed; fast memory and caches supported.
 - Quick manual, source code and icons by Exoticons and Chris Vella included.
 - Optional Enhanced framerate for the PAL 0658 and NTSC 1489 releases.

 Options:
 --------
 CUSTOM1=1: Enhanced framerate (default: off).
 Runs the world at its intended pace while updating controls and helicopter
 motion more frequently. Other moving objects are drawn smoothly between
 world updates. Weapons launch on the next world update. On a 68000 this
 option is ignored and native timing is retained.

 CUSTOM4=0: CPU renderer (default when Enhanced framerate is enabled).
 CUSTOM4=1: Original blitter renderer.
 The renderer choice only applies with CUSTOM1=1. The CPU renderer needs
 about 36 KB of additional free fast memory; if unavailable, drawing falls
 back to the blitter. All framerate enhancements share the CUSTOM1 switch.

 The installer uses Gunship.slave for PAL 0658 and GunshipNTSC.slave for
 NTSC 1489. Choose by the game release, not by your Amiga's video mode.
 Other previously supported releases retain native timing. Their enhanced
 timing has not been ported or tested; the German and alternate title
 releases were not available for this beta's tests.

 Beta notes:
 -----------
 Enhanced mode is still awaiting full-mission play-testing on the A1200 and
 68060. The unattended demo uses original timing and controls even when
 Enhanced framerate is enabled.
 The reported 68060 T-74 identification-screen graphics issue remains open.
 The 68040 graphics corruption caused by unfinished blitter clears has been
 fixed in enhanced mode. CACHE works in the tested full-MMU FS-UAE setup;
 a cycle-exact NOMMU workaround is no longer required. In that emulator
 profile, select CUSTOM4=1 for better speed. Real 68040 hardware has not
 been tested.

 History:
 --------
 version 2.0b (21.10.2026) done by Vesa Halttunen:
 - optional smoother framerate and responsive controls on 68020 and later
 - selectable faster CPU renderer
 - fixes for enhanced-mode ground climb indication, missile kills and
   small-bank left drift; damage-flash background colour restores correctly
 - smoother damaged-tail-rotor turning; 68040 graphics corruption fixed
 - updated installer with PAL/NTSC selection

 version 1.2 (15.02.2020) done by JOTD:
 - another original version supported (from which the supported crack was issued)

 version 1.1 (12.09.05) done by JOTD:
 - another version (without MPS logo) supported & fixed (needs re-installing)

 version 1.0 (10.01.05) done by JOTD:
 - initial release
 - 3 versions supported, 2 originals & 1 crack
 - disk & password protections removed on original versions
 - access fault fixed
 - use of fastmem & caches for awesome speed
 - nice icons by Exoticons & Chris Vella
 - quick manual included
 - source code included


 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
